IMPORT `ref-guarded`

§ `Nine coverage queries against the guarded encoding`

-- One maker so every claim below is built the same way and only the fields a
-- query actually speaks to are varied.  Everything not named by a query is set
-- to the value that lets the policy apply, per the standing preamble.
GIVEN ground   IS A `Hospitalization Ground`
      hosp     IS A NUMBER
      age      IS A NUMBER
      causes   IS A LIST OF Cause
      visit    IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      conf     IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      fraud    IS A BOOLEAN
      misrep   IS A BOOLEAN
      withheld IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Claim
`a claim` ground hosp age causes visit conf fraud misrep withheld MEANS
  Claim WITH
    `the hospitalization was for` IS ground
    `month of the hospitalization` IS hosp
    `age at the time of the hospitalization` IS age
    `the event arose directly or indirectly out of` IS causes
    `this agreement is signed` IS TRUE
    `the applicable premium for the policy period has been paid` IS TRUE
    `month the wellness visit occurred` IS visit
    `month written confirmation of the visit was supplied` IS conf
    `there is fraud` IS fraud
    `there is a misrepresentation of information provided to the Company` IS misrep
    `there is a material withholding of information provided to the Company` IS withheld
    `a dispute or disagreement has arisen` IS FALSE
    `month the parties were unable to settle the dispute` IS NOTHING
    `month arbitration was commenced` IS NOTHING
    `a valid arbitration award has been issued` IS FALSE
    `month written proof of claim was submitted` IS NOTHING
    `month recovery on the policy is sought` IS NOTHING

`no named cause` MEANS LIST `a cause not named in clause 2.1`

-- Q1: burns suffered while doing my duty as a firefighter.
`Q1 claim` MEANS `a claim` `accidental injury` 8 40 (LIST `service as a fire fighter`) (JUST 6) (JUST 7) FALSE FALSE FALSE
#EVAL `benefit is payable` `Q1 claim`

-- Q2: 78 years old at the time of hospitalization.
`Q2 claim` MEANS `a claim` sickness 8 78 `no named cause` (JUST 6) (JUST 7) FALSE FALSE FALSE
#EVAL `benefit is payable` `Q2 claim`

-- Q3: pneumonia, hospitalized month 5, age 65.
`Q3 claim` MEANS `a claim` sickness 5 65 `no named cause` (JUST 3) (JUST 4) FALSE FALSE FALSE
#EVAL `benefit is payable` `Q3 claim`

-- Q4: fall while travelling abroad; confirmation supplied at month 8.
--     Hospitalization month is not named by the query, so it is set to the
--     value that lets the policy apply (month 7 -- 1.3 is then still pending).
`Q4 claim` MEANS `a claim` `accidental injury` 7 40 `no named cause` (JUST 6) (JUST 8) FALSE FALSE FALSE
#EVAL `benefit is payable` `Q4 claim`

-- Q4b: the same claim with the hospitalization at month 9 instead, i.e. after
--      the month-7 confirmation deadline had passed.
`Q4b claim` MEANS `a claim` `accidental injury` 9 40 `no named cause` (JUST 6) (JUST 8) FALSE FALSE FALSE
#EVAL `benefit is payable` `Q4b claim`

-- Q5: punching my own face to show off; no fraud, no misrepresentation.
--     A deliberately self-inflicted blow is neither sickness nor accidental
--     injury.
`Q5 claim` MEANS `a claim` `neither sickness nor accidental injury` 8 40 `no named cause` (JUST 6) (JUST 7) FALSE FALSE FALSE
#EVAL `benefit is payable` `Q5 claim`

-- Q5b: the same claim read instead as an accidental injury.
`Q5b claim` MEANS `a claim` `accidental injury` 8 40 `no named cause` (JUST 6) (JUST 7) FALSE FALSE FALSE
#EVAL `benefit is payable` `Q5b claim`

-- Q6: skydiving injury, age 79, confirmation supplied at month 6.5.
`Q6 claim` MEANS `a claim` `accidental injury` 7 79 (LIST skydiving) (JUST 6) (JUST 6.5) FALSE FALSE FALSE
#EVAL `benefit is payable` `Q6 claim`

-- Q7: heart attack, confirmation supplied at month 2, age 75.
`Q7 claim` MEANS `a claim` sickness 3 75 `no named cause` (JUST 1) (JUST 2) FALSE FALSE FALSE
#EVAL `benefit is payable` `Q7 claim`

-- Q8: injured in a military training exercise, inside the term, no fraud.
`Q8 claim` MEANS `a claim` `accidental injury` 8 40 (LIST `service in the military`) (JUST 6) (JUST 7) FALSE FALSE FALSE
#EVAL `benefit is payable` `Q8 claim`

-- Q9: bitten in the ankle by my son; confirmation supplied at month 6; I was
--     serving as a police officer at the time.  The bite does not arise
--     directly or indirectly out of police service, so 2.1(4) is not engaged.
`Q9 claim` MEANS `a claim` `accidental injury` 7 40 `no named cause` (JUST 6) (JUST 6) FALSE FALSE FALSE
#EVAL `benefit is payable` `Q9 claim`

-- Q9b: the same claim read instead as arising out of service in the police.
`Q9b claim` MEANS `a claim` `accidental injury` 7 40 (LIST `service in the police`) (JUST 6) (JUST 6) FALSE FALSE FALSE
#EVAL `benefit is payable` `Q9b claim`
